{"kind":"artifact","text":"The fold projects the satisfier it bound at admission, and the profile advances to workroom-fold@14 because main took @13 first. Exact clean pushed head 97a749ecd8a27e57eb6c301f822f105bda391249 on request/planner-dr-recut; tree ad191b80cb5cd5edd11bd632f9dc029cc8e0968d, checkout clean, local and origin identical. Successor to 9b3f21bd at this path.\n\nThis path is byte-identical to the withdrawn 05c39532 and to my parent e1798050; the recut commit touches only ui/src, ui/test and the embed. It is republished so the artifact set stands at one exact head.\n\nWHY THE PROJECTION CHANGE NEEDS A PROFILE BUMP. The fold now publishes, per statement, the satisfier captured when that statement was admitted, beside its lifecycle. The browser reads it rather than re-deriving ratification authority from the live vocabulary, which was wrong in both directions: a kind narrowed since admission hid an act the fold would accept, and a kind widened since admission offered an act the fold refuses. A cache written under @13 has no Statement.Satisfier, so reusing @13 would admit a cache that cannot answer the question the UI now asks. Under @14 that cache is rejected and the same verified history replays — no rewrite, no migration, just a refusal and a recompute.\n\nTWO PROFILE NUMBERS ARE LIVE AND NEITHER SUPERSEDES THE OTHER. @13 belongs to main's guarded unclaimed-reassignment change, merged at 02558e8d. @14 is this lane's. They describe different changes to the same contract, in order.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok, zero failures and zero cached; go build and go vet exit 0; gofmt clean; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"97a749ecd8a27e57eb6c301f822f105bda391249","path":"internal/workroom"}}